<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Electric Motorbike Short vs Long-Term Rental Cost in Hanoi: Cost Planning Guide</h1>
<p>The electric motorbike rents in Hanoi at three verified structures: 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week, and 1,500,000 VND per month, a single published monthly figure rather than a range. This guide compares short-term against long-term cost so the calendar, not habit, picks the rate.</p>
<p>We put all three rates side by side, find the break-even points at five days and ten days, show what each structure is actually for, list the mistakes that cost money on both ends of the scale, and close with the deposit, gear and charging questions that long stays add. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, see the full model range at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and check common questions on the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The three verified rates</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">What short-term cost looks like</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">What long-term cost looks like</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The break-even at five days</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">The break-even at ten days</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-6">Riding the electric short versus long</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-7">Agreements, deposits and support</a></li>
